{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "independent_source_only": true,
  "source_proof_scope": "C.1 compact smooth C.2 and density/closedness toward B.13; actual B.1/B.9 law contracts",
  "inventory": [
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p1.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4573,
      "line_end": 4576,
      "byte_start": 1003091,
      "byte_end": 1004181,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p1.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "f7df116ca00ea43aba42880206caa3bf0ecf88ea40ce226a95c642de7cef3a43",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "We first prove\n(B.13). It suffices to consider\n$f\\in C_{\\rm c}^{\\infty}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})$, the general case following by density and\nclosedness of the gradient."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p2.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4579,
      "line_end": 4580,
      "byte_start": 1004227,
      "byte_end": 1005045,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p2.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "ce63fe21e27606ed10bcd07a7af1a80c070107702bd6c4a31587e6b388b5054b",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Recall that the conditional\ndensity $p_{y}$ of $Y_{-}$ given $Y_{+}=y$ is"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4581,
      "line_end": 4587,
      "byte_start": 1005046,
      "byte_end": 1006546,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "a6e23d867da3c53566002b685501788ae4341e97b8838c6cb5dab6a8f06a8db4",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$p_{y}(u)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V((y+u)/2)-\\frac{\\|y-u\\|^{2}}{8\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,,$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p2.2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4588,
      "line_end": 4588,
      "byte_start": 1006547,
      "byte_end": 1006644,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p2.2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "8a5c59a780c4a2610c1fdb5bc8cf1d99cc7a90a7d4b72ce281ddccbc3ee9237e",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "and define"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4589,
      "line_end": 4595,
      "byte_start": 1006645,
      "byte_end": 1007876,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "eac5ef047f3caac97461376e3dff8d0bb8f5cb225c7dfb90a49f89b65636fb24",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$s_{y}(u)\\coloneqq-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\nabla V((y+u)/2)-\\frac{y-u}{4\\eta}\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p2.3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4596,
      "line_end": 4596,
      "byte_start": 1007877,
      "byte_end": 1008020,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p2.3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "7e354547d57734848863d271f457961e2e4ba8184ab074e6b2b99047c2304a4e",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Differentiating the normalized conditional density gives"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.E1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4597,
      "line_end": 4604,
      "byte_start": 1008021,
      "byte_end": 1009588,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.E1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "758bde8e1d0c478a89e978bd88b4a0d84d0c82ad2309ecca8b16b4511b438e33",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\\mathrm{Cov}\\bigl(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\\bigm|Y_{+}=y\\bigr)\\,.$\n\n(C.1)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p3.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4607,
      "line_end": 4607,
      "byte_start": 1009634,
      "byte_end": 1009975,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p3.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "da145ff5b2728858aa9d129117115fac6ff44ff1d038aed5a1edaa677b78aed1",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "The negative log-density of $p_{y}$ has Hessian"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4608,
      "line_end": 4614,
      "byte_start": 1009976,
      "byte_end": 1011557,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "7b3635bea6311fb5b5ca2a7ede1a2461dde8e8098c79d2ea0c7dd23f4ab7d95e",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\bigl\\{\\nabla^{2}V((y+u)/2)+\\eta^{-1}I\\bigr\\}\\succeq\\frac{\\alpha+\\eta^{-1}}{4}\\,I\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p3.2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4615,
      "line_end": 4616,
      "byte_start": 1011558,
      "byte_end": 1011904,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p3.2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "ace3b7d8f20c18c8b9c2754b1fde29807c0371e939cc3ba4bbd1e3b584f57337",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Hence, the conditional Poincaré inequality implies, for every unit\nvector $a$,"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.EGx24",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4617,
      "line_end": 4624,
      "byte_start": 1011905,
      "byte_end": 1014655,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.EGx24.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "0019c155f2ceec2eae8e9ae1e0ef12fdb5927cd5e0df50e651d59add5027fb8e",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\displaystyle\\Var\\bigl(a^{\\top}s_{y}(Y_{-})\\bigm|Y_{+}=y\\bigr)$\n$\\displaystyle\\leq\\frac{4}{\\alpha+\\eta^{-1}}\\,\\mathbb{E}\\bigl[\\|\\nabla_{u}(a^{\\top}s_{y})(Y_{-})\\|^{2}\\,\\bigm|\\,Y_{+}=y\\bigr]\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p3.3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4625,
      "line_end": 4627,
      "byte_start": 1014656,
      "byte_end": 1015585,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p3.3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "b0e5d9ad809ddea45b881f16a4c83161fd17118c2ad410037f4dbd4681434a4b",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "The assumptions\n$\\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V\\preceq\\beta I$ and\n$\\beta\\eta\\leq 1$ give"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex5",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4628,
      "line_end": 4634,
      "byte_start": 1015586,
      "byte_end": 1016685,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex5.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "4d27c57c448e791bf3731ab1c2be1cae1265d020845b62e1bf1602c2370620cb",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\|\\nabla_{u}s_{y}(u)\\|_{\\rm op}\\leq\\frac{\\eta^{-1}-\\alpha}{4}\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p3.4",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4635,
      "line_end": 4635,
      "byte_start": 1016686,
      "byte_end": 1016786,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p3.4.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "69e031e2db49a75b2ecdfa58f113b8afa5372b494685aedb748423b97c61cfd1",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Consequently,"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex6",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4636,
      "line_end": 4642,
      "byte_start": 1016787,
      "byte_end": 1018499,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex6.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "d979fb9a8cc56871a34c4092adb99c918843f02b7a514b1b1ab9dc3ce36a9212",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\Var\\bigl(a^{\\top}s_{y}(Y_{-})\\bigm|Y_{+}=y\\bigr)\\leq\\frac{(\\eta^{-1}-\\alpha)^{2}}{4\\,(\\alpha+\\eta^{-1})}\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p3.5",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4643,
      "line_end": 4645,
      "byte_start": 1018500,
      "byte_end": 1019260,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p3.5.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "0493bd11bf7ed924f4b54e6a347990927b65e476bd1e36c07b60874a05b60937",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Applying conditional Cauchy–Schwarz in\n(C.1) and taking the supremum over\n$\\|a\\|=1$ yields"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex7",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4646,
      "line_end": 4652,
      "byte_start": 1019261,
      "byte_end": 1021061,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex7.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "5127afc363889fda877a295746bd75315f42881850cd1fe45dc8501ea7f56af0",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\|\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f(y)\\|^{2}\\leq\\frac{(\\eta^{-1}-\\alpha)^{2}}{4\\,(\\alpha+\\eta^{-1})}\\Var(f(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+}=y)\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p3.6",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4653,
      "line_end": 4653,
      "byte_start": 1021062,
      "byte_end": 1021690,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p3.6.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "2bb922677ff77b9ffa80336474a642f6f14ad85dd7d6a89be304ffe2558290f6",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Integrating in $y$ and using (B.9),"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.EGx25",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4654,
      "line_end": 4661,
      "byte_start": 1021691,
      "byte_end": 1023696,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.EGx25.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "0465aa325855b3a5d0be03edb900467fc6299804cc676bee9421429ca88de0a3",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\displaystyle\\eta\\,\\|\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\leq\\frac{(1-\\alpha\\eta)^{2}}{4\\,(1+\\alpha\\eta)}\\,\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\,.$\n\n(C.2)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p3.7",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "compact-smooth C.1/C.2 and unnamed rough-input density/closedness route",
      "line_start": 4662,
      "line_end": 4664,
      "byte_start": 1023697,
      "byte_end": 1025470,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p3.7.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "f0a4fb9b16fdb080566654ff1609d4633c82fd28090baa03db99562fa7a53fee",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Finally,\n$\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\|f\\|^{2}-\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}$,\nwhich proves (B.13)."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p4.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4667,
      "line_end": 4669,
      "byte_start": 1025516,
      "byte_end": 1027227,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p4.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "d1ef31fc9ae67dc514ed545cf36ca858dbfcd931d870e367e2c3901bc227aa72",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "We next bound the spectrum of $\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}$. Let $f\\in\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}$.\nSince $\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}$ preserves constants, $\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f$ is centered.\nThe Poincaré inequality for the marginal law $\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}$ gives"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.E3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4670,
      "line_end": 4677,
      "byte_start": 1027228,
      "byte_end": 1029036,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.E3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "d3751b92957e3cd1d4b24d08a74d8631a7574cc23a58587aaaf2c9b176c1344b",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\Var_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}}(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f)\\leq\\Bigl(\\frac{1}{\\alpha}+\\eta\\Bigr)\\,\\|\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\,.$\n\n(C.3)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p4.2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4678,
      "line_end": 4679,
      "byte_start": 1029037,
      "byte_end": 1029754,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p4.2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "4690dce06a8facb2df6a6b7f8eca0ed38f8e70cb0088876a244546cec2630aa9",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Combining (C.3) with\n(C.2) and rearranging gives"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.E4",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4680,
      "line_end": 4687,
      "byte_start": 1029755,
      "byte_end": 1031371,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.E4.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "832e5eba8dbe8fd2b0361f4514814d7e6462b20418b04693badb9aa6122ce341",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|\\leq\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,\\|f\\|=\\rho_{\\rm mac}\\,\\|f\\|\\,.$\n\n(C.4)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p4.3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4688,
      "line_end": 4688,
      "byte_start": 1031372,
      "byte_end": 1031774,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p4.3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "b93e0ad9d63b1b1219348b0225d1dbe0284b39e0583d6557001522d060aea20c",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Since $\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}$ is self-adjoint, this proves"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex8",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4689,
      "line_end": 4695,
      "byte_start": 1031775,
      "byte_end": 1032741,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex8.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "c22e0d3c07b7f3862407e319cd45a72093c5eb3ad4b5bb184133ad999fa38f14",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$-\\rho_{\\rm mac}I\\preceq\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\preceq\\rho_{\\rm mac}I\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p4.4",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4696,
      "line_end": 4699,
      "byte_start": 1032742,
      "byte_end": 1034183,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p4.4.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "c989b8174926e58914d8c3853312b96d9dadc4edd64c4363c8a25093992bc474",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "It remains only to obtain the uniform lower bound\n$\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\succeq-\\frac{1}{2}\\,I$.\nFor every $g\\in H^{1}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})$, exchangeability and\n(B.8) give"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.EGx26",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4700,
      "line_end": 4708,
      "byte_start": 1034184,
      "byte_end": 1037760,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.EGx26.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "b5ac86540d70e846fd94fbf609d8088ef9f1a6746a69aea2533df694a54ab17a",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\displaystyle\\bigl\\langle g,(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})g\\bigr\\rangle$\n$\\displaystyle=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathbb{E}\\bigl[\\bigl(g(Y_{+})-g(Y_{-})\\bigr)^{2}\\bigr]=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{X}\\mathbb{E}_{Z}\\bigl[\\bigl(g(X+\\sqrt{\\eta}Z)-g(X-\\sqrt{\\eta}Z)\\bigr)^{2}\\bigr]\\,.$\n\n(C.5)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p4.5",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4709,
      "line_end": 4709,
      "byte_start": 1037761,
      "byte_end": 1038121,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p4.5.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "71ddf1f8b92fce238d43bbca93a97ced3ea85ebd928b7b174066a3423e15f60b",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "For fixed $X=x$, the Gaussian Poincaré inequality implies"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.EGx27",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4710,
      "line_end": 4717,
      "byte_start": 1038122,
      "byte_end": 1041024,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.EGx27.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "47e92e67e2f988b9be14caf82b1afb717f211dfd91fce05ec352662eb34465db",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\displaystyle\\mathbb{E}_{Z}\\bigl[\\bigl(g(x+\\sqrt{\\eta}Z)-g(x-\\sqrt{\\eta}Z)\\bigr)^{2}\\bigr]$\n$\\displaystyle\\leq\\eta\\,\\mathbb{E}_{Z}\\bigl\\|\\nabla g(x+\\sqrt{\\eta}Z)+\\nabla g(x-\\sqrt{\\eta}Z)\\bigr\\|^{2}\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p4.6",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4718,
      "line_end": 4719,
      "byte_start": 1041025,
      "byte_end": 1041791,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p4.6.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "0d6c650a4c4d4862886afb733d1f6d664f96ea2c94fc6ab3c7f1dacc61d56abb",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Averaging in $X$ and using that $Y_{+}$ and $Y_{-}$ have the same\nmarginal gives"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.E6",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4720,
      "line_end": 4727,
      "byte_start": 1041792,
      "byte_end": 1043304,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.E6.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "6c96bcd0743dff97b53b652fb11a261cdebb3b36127a6699374150ab31b21e3d",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\bigl\\langle g,(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})g\\bigr\\rangle\\leq 2\\eta\\,\\|\\nabla g\\|^{2}\\,.$\n\n(C.6)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p5.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4730,
      "line_end": 4731,
      "byte_start": 1043350,
      "byte_end": 1044532,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p5.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "dc50ebf2ba72dba6d81404949c46fea9cf258af9d5d8ad12d7feaaaeeb91c8c3",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Applying (C.6) with $g=\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f$ and using\n(B.13), we obtain"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.EGx28",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4732,
      "line_end": 4739,
      "byte_start": 1044533,
      "byte_end": 1047668,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.EGx28.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "f5d03e3b96c917e70d44e80ee1e75dfcf9d202dcae5cf52c0b6bab26164e4db8",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\displaystyle\\bigl\\langle f,\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})f\\bigr\\rangle$\n$\\displaystyle=\\bigl\\langle\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f,(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\bigr\\rangle\\leq 2\\eta\\,\\|\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\leq\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\bigl\\langle f,(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2})f\\bigr\\rangle\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p5.2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4740,
      "line_end": 4741,
      "byte_start": 1047669,
      "byte_end": 1048643,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p5.2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "a7f9afd11d06aec7f5fcd885f87a2cdf2b25158a62ac3754d4d7a5d07f7d938d",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Thus, as an operator inequality, $2\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})\\preceq I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}$,\nor equivalently"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.E7",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4742,
      "line_end": 4749,
      "byte_start": 1048644,
      "byte_end": 1049943,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.E7.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "8cbc609e2f04c60179a9e747cb2c907588f754fa2d7b39c5efb6b0c27655262b",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})^{2}(I+2\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})\\succeq 0\\,.$\n\n(C.7)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p5.3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4750,
      "line_end": 4752,
      "byte_start": 1049944,
      "byte_end": 1051028,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p5.3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "a51a5ce18bbdcb94ae76c86170eac3d847cd2ab25e12e06b9fc9545903b8199c",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Since $\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}$ is a self-adjoint contraction, its spectrum lies in\n$[-1,1]$. The scalar inequality corresponding to\n(C.7) is"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex11",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4753,
      "line_end": 4759,
      "byte_start": 1051029,
      "byte_end": 1052411,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex11.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "8942670fc31adbcf5326e87496d3cec4c017ea56fbd3fdf0fa01ba517665c692",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$(1-\\lambda)^{2}(1+2\\lambda)\\geq 0\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\lambda\\in\\operatorname{Spec}(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})\\,,$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p5.4",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4760,
      "line_end": 4763,
      "byte_start": 1052412,
      "byte_end": 1054329,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p5.4.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "afc9fa17dbb94cbdd547c7ea2cf71c4df7d2c9eedbad77c2704b834d8a71b069",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "and therefore $\\operatorname{Spec}(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}})\\subseteq[-1/2,1]$. Hence\n$-\\frac{1}{2}I\\,\\preceq\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}$.\nTogether with (C.4), this proves\n(B.14)."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p6.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4766,
      "line_end": 4766,
      "byte_start": 1054375,
      "byte_end": 1054470,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p6.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "821579c42959b326cea3fb9ef8d102a629d71a327c2018c2833ec6bc870cc072",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Finally,"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex12",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4767,
      "line_end": 4773,
      "byte_start": 1054471,
      "byte_end": 1056144,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex12.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "4032d43b7e291d8d287fc89ad35c2d0d430f447da59d95880cf86cec7f565a55",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\succeq(1-\\rho_{\\rm mac}^{2})\\,I=\\frac{4\\alpha\\eta}{(1+\\alpha\\eta)^{2}}\\,I\\,,$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p6.2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4774,
      "line_end": 4774,
      "byte_start": 1056145,
      "byte_end": 1056245,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p6.2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "38fb787827fbb13090ccd6f02b3166a813cf078077f83ade106673800305498b",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "and therefore"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex13",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4775,
      "line_end": 4781,
      "byte_start": 1056246,
      "byte_end": 1057513,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex13.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "85adbececf2e41a842155bc3eb5c23eb84a8b5ad2acfce7285c826cbfe003f36",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\succeq\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta}}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,I=\\gamma_{\\rm gap}I\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p6.3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "B.14/B.15 spectral-coercivity continuation; distinct conclusion outside rough-gradient56 slice",
      "line_start": 4782,
      "line_end": 4783,
      "byte_start": 1057514,
      "byte_end": 1058000,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p6.3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "de66b544c2a9c5089be2a100f4b0cdb1cf0494bf24b2492c2b6eb911782176a8",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "This proves (B.15).\n∎"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p7.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4787,
      "line_end": 4788,
      "byte_start": 1058053,
      "byte_end": 1058456,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p7.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "1482a70e808dbf294400cd7b6dd9bb2427ccc1f2a76adeb14f03555eb4736890",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "The half-turn analysis below uses the following alternative form of\n(C.1)."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4793,
      "line_end": 4793,
      "byte_start": 1059194,
      "byte_end": 1060260,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "bead52108817cbff63514159eb5c1aa937bcbbb9e55f1a1b0de001cdf2ae4d44",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "For every $f\\in H^{1}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})$ and $\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}$-almost every $y$,"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.E8",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4794,
      "line_end": 4801,
      "byte_start": 1060261,
      "byte_end": 1062104,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.E8.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "ea8867c091141a43d34fae5b7a95b6e80f1da52b290292cd0a5777a97bf6cb74",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\\mathbb{E}[\\nabla f(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+}=y]-\\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\\nabla V(X)\\mid Y_{+}=y)\\,.$\n\n(C.8)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p8.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4807,
      "line_end": 4808,
      "byte_start": 1062271,
      "byte_end": 1063200,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p8.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "67701025230595cd872be914bce7bc59932119dfed2deb2c0226fe31b1c905ee",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "First let $f\\in C_{\\rm c}^{\\infty}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})$. The representation\n(C.1) gives"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex14",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4809,
      "line_end": 4815,
      "byte_start": 1063201,
      "byte_end": 1064505,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex14.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "35462a02938eeab40967d959ed9bbfe08139cfad72e47740b4a84bbb54661de7",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+}=y)\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p8.2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4816,
      "line_end": 4816,
      "byte_start": 1064506,
      "byte_end": 1064841,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p8.2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "f1bbd6720028c09b81152520c176c1b51f4e3299155c5cc8a09a2fdbbc8429ff",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Using the definition of $s_{y}$, we write"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex15",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4817,
      "line_end": 4823,
      "byte_start": 1064842,
      "byte_end": 1066417,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex15.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "b2579aabbdc60d67e5b964ae2b9d818e9c7fb5550c5abd80fac3ca15c2844613",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$s_{y}(u)=\\Bigl\\{\\frac{1}{2}\\nabla V((y+u)/2)-\\frac{y-u}{4\\eta}\\Bigr\\}-\\nabla V((y+u)/2)\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p8.3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4824,
      "line_end": 4826,
      "byte_start": 1066418,
      "byte_end": 1067369,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p8.3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "cbe2389fd25c618e512a3c4bcf55dcd3d3814f9fe5f9613f0626288585462ed2",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "To rewrite (C.1) in the claimed form, we\nonly need to identify the covariance generated by the vector in braces.\nIntegration by parts in $u$ against the conditional density $p_{y}$ gives"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.E9",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4827,
      "line_end": 4834,
      "byte_start": 1067370,
      "byte_end": 1069516,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.E9.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "443ae429fe07399ce3f808e46bd37a7ce6485a22b34d4943a5158e45e0995552",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\mathbb{E}[\\nabla f(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+}=y]=\\mathbb{E}\\Bigl[f(Y_{-})\\,\\Bigl\\{\\frac{1}{2}\\nabla V(X)-\\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\ \\Bigm|\\ Y_{+}=y\\Bigr]\\,.$\n\n(C.9)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p8.4",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4835,
      "line_end": 4836,
      "byte_start": 1069517,
      "byte_end": 1070390,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p8.4.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "4d6278e96e463f7a8e4c509a253350e43533021620ac3257461f9dcd4a0f118b",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Applying (C.9) to $f\\equiv 1$, justified by compactly\nsupported cutoffs converging to $1$, gives"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex16",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4837,
      "line_end": 4843,
      "byte_start": 1070391,
      "byte_end": 1071721,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex16.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "646e1228195166aedc987c277da3f2aa715ff8cccdb471864de70fdb5896a90c",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\mathbb{E}\\Bigl[\\frac{1}{2}\\nabla V(X)-\\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\\eta}\\,\\Bigm|\\,Y_{+}=y\\Bigr]=0\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p8.5",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4844,
      "line_end": 4844,
      "byte_start": 1071722,
      "byte_end": 1072132,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p8.5.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "ab061a8379d0c280a2577948dbe9074625e1ea7799dbff915449791e3570990d",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Combining this with (C.9), we obtain"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.EGx29",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4845,
      "line_end": 4862,
      "byte_start": 1072133,
      "byte_end": 1078677,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.EGx29.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "ba20545e3967d6c8858a1e52e338ddb52c12189e2c82f601556da827a07fac49",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\displaystyle\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f(y)$\n$\\displaystyle=\\mathrm{Cov}\\Bigl(f(Y_{-}),\\frac{1}{2}\\nabla V(X)-\\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\\eta}\\,\\Bigm|\\,Y_{+}=y\\Bigr)-\\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\\nabla V(X)\\mid Y_{+}=y)$\n\n\n\n\n$\\displaystyle=\\mathbb{E}\\Bigl[f(Y_{-})\\,\\Bigl\\{\\frac{1}{2}\\nabla V(X)-\\frac{y-Y_{-}}{4\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\Bigm|\\,Y_{+}=y\\Bigr]-\\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\\nabla V(X)\\mid Y_{+}=y)$\n\n\n\n\n$\\displaystyle=\\mathbb{E}[\\nabla f(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+}=y]-\\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\\nabla V(X)\\mid Y_{+}=y)\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p8.6",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4863,
      "line_end": 4863,
      "byte_start": 1078678,
      "byte_end": 1079304,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p8.6.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "9844704eb25922c96f6e88dfd8e697cc76d5f44a824263fe47ae2d1a32570c2c",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "This is (C.8) for smooth $f$."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p9.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4866,
      "line_end": 4871,
      "byte_start": 1079350,
      "byte_end": 1081809,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p9.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "6af4fa8f23bbae53148753f073716da0925784e0ca9fcb6ddfd5a3b469f410b2",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "The extension to $H^{1}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})$ is a standard approximation\nargument once we check that the covariance term is continuous in\n$L^{2}$. By (2.11), the conditional\nlaw of $X$ given $Y_{+}=y$ has Poincaré constant at most\n$\\eta/(1+\\alpha\\eta)\\leq\\eta$. Hence, for every unit vector\n$a\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}$,"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex20",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4872,
      "line_end": 4878,
      "byte_start": 1081810,
      "byte_end": 1083453,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex20.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "a8f8b66f674a113f7f3fb3f5e4f87c037ffebdff62b4ebb47292241fea57aa71",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\Var(a^{\\top}\\nabla V(X)\\mid Y_{+}=y)\\leq\\eta\\,\\mathbb{E}[\\|\\nabla^{2}V(X)\\,a\\|^{2}\\mid Y_{+}=y]\\leq\\beta^{2}\\eta\\,.$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p9.2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4879,
      "line_end": 4880,
      "byte_start": 1083454,
      "byte_end": 1083921,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p9.2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "bf2902fc6270c74948d9986c3c55c589094e75e5d5201d2a3d90dcc419ce35a0",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Conditional Cauchy–Schwarz and\n(B.9) therefore imply"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.Ex21",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4881,
      "line_end": 4887,
      "byte_start": 1083922,
      "byte_end": 1085764,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.Ex21.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "8bbb2c0e6ee209cfe68a82892b05734f385cc5b34e75b5d8e37e23e9added348",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\bigl\\|\\mathrm{Cov}(f(Y_{-}),\\nabla V(X)\\mid Y_{+})\\bigr\\|_{L^{2}}\\leq\\beta\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|\\,,$"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A3.SS1.p9.3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Lemma C.1/C.8 derivative identity for H1 input; distinct half-turn consumer, not a premise of rough-L2 B.13",
      "line_start": 4888,
      "line_end": 4893,
      "byte_start": 1085765,
      "byte_end": 1088089,
      "balanced_fragment": "A3.SS1.p9.3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "0f412bfd29098492e56658e1c4e22b9fc5c2324786c0b493479ff775a098a696",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "and the same bound applies to differences. Conditional expectation is\nan $L^{2}$ contraction, and (B.13) controls the\nleft side. Thus every term in (C.8) is\ncontinuous under $H^{1}$ approximation. Density of\n$C_{\\rm c}^{\\infty}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})$ in $H^{1}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})$ completes the proof.\n∎"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S1.p1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 350,
      "line_end": 363,
      "byte_start": 47126,
      "byte_end": 50729,
      "balanced_fragment": "S1.p1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "a9bc657fb926368561ab2657dfbfbf6a7a0ba5b8c2122f8d1fb8510a0a975262",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "We study the problem of sampling from the probability measure\n$\\mu(\\mathrm{d}x)=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$ on $\\mathbb{R}^{d}$, where\n$V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})$ satisfies, for $0<\\alpha\\leq\\beta$,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n$\\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptx\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\kappa\\coloneqq\\tfrac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,.$\n\n(1.1)\n\n\n\nThe main result of this paper is the following."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S1.E1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 354,
      "line_end": 361,
      "byte_start": 49052,
      "byte_end": 50640,
      "balanced_fragment": "S1.E1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "b5c735fec9494c1dfb15f345b7ccf9c4352e80842308f3e62cc360e36ea2872f",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptx\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\kappa\\coloneqq\\tfrac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,.$\n\n(1.1)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.SS2.p1.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 614,
      "line_end": 616,
      "byte_start": 95559,
      "byte_end": 96221,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.SS2.p1.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "32f65c3fd7b7b1bb4d250acfacbcd6a719e46c43f9d23bc4c821fc67f4c55ef7",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Our algorithm operates on the augmented distribution underlying the\nproximal sampler of Lee, Shen, and Tian [17]. For a\nscale $\\eta\\in(0,1/\\beta]$, consider the joint law"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.E6",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 617,
      "line_end": 624,
      "byte_start": 96222,
      "byte_end": 98215,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.E6.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "1f01e27c8eb38fd05a57d820c65ee6b36832171cce845e8cd1b52f4588526375",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\pi_{\\eta}(\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\,.$\n\n(2.6)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.E7",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 627,
      "line_end": 634,
      "byte_start": 98826,
      "byte_end": 100299,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.E7.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "2be554d84baf1f2b796ade05fba49271b5d05e4e8d2d46427d47a6756f85c8f9",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$X\\sim\\mu\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptZ\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)\\ \\text{independently}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptY=X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,.$\n\n(2.7)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.SS2.p1.3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 635,
      "line_end": 640,
      "byte_start": 100300,
      "byte_end": 103210,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.SS2.p1.3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "88acd72591b34c91b79748a608c4055defcc626177d46412bb70d6de7b478c32",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "Its $X$-marginal is $\\pi_{\\eta}^{X}=\\mu$. Write $\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}$ for\nthe $Y$-marginal, so that\n$\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}(\\mathrm{d}y)\\propto e^{-U_{\\eta}(y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y$; by\n(2.7), $\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}=\\mu*\\mathcal{N}(0,\\eta I)$\nis a Gaussian smoothing of the target.\nWe use superscripts for marginal and conditional laws; in particular,"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.E8",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 641,
      "line_end": 648,
      "byte_start": 103211,
      "byte_end": 105641,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.E8.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "f72b9e301f7145614d1dcdad5cba42f06d2b7a1723a29fa65b1f16555b238584",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y\\mid X=x}=\\mathcal{N}(x,\\eta I)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,.$\n\n(2.8)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.E9",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 679,
      "line_end": 686,
      "byte_start": 110677,
      "byte_end": 111985,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.E9.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "0eee1430d82a367d693bd62e4adfd8f9d8926c7ad2998204ad7801f47231728f",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$V_{y}(x)\\coloneqq V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\,.$\n\n(2.9)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.E10",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 688,
      "line_end": 695,
      "byte_start": 112130,
      "byte_end": 113641,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.E10.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "540ecdc7b0e82cfb6c35e2be696b9237b8211b2a0fa99b4fc7b0efd4fc765347",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$(\\alpha+\\eta^{-1})I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V_{y}(x)\\preceq(\\beta+\\eta^{-1})I\\,,$\n\n(2.10)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.E11",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 699,
      "line_end": 706,
      "byte_start": 114783,
      "byte_end": 116492,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.E11.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "b5c67354e00bad60bacdd95d7c3be5368517a600f52898c56493f12393c160fb",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\Var_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(f)\\leq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}\\|\\nabla f\\|^{2}\\,,$\n\n(2.11)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.E13",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 720,
      "line_end": 727,
      "byte_start": 118748,
      "byte_end": 120244,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.E13.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "4f6cbd321e24190b27ea072854778d84c8ba6fe379ec56dae884115e04559cfc",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\frac{\\alpha}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}U_{\\eta}(y)\\preceq\\frac{\\beta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\,.$\n\n(2.13)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.E14",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 732,
      "line_end": 739,
      "byte_start": 120545,
      "byte_end": 121631,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.E14.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "9f6da2cb937646e03fb86a374e38fd8b61ca39cbcdc8306bd6aa89782fde8bb6",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\mathsf{U}:(x,y)\\mapsto(x,2x-y)$\n\n(2.14)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "S2.SS2.p3.1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 746,
      "line_end": 754,
      "byte_start": 122137,
      "byte_end": 125049,
      "balanced_fragment": "S2.SS2.p3.1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "cb3970f6f8fb24e28bec639bfe6a0c46cf83784b3134e6dab9e07337db24c18e",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "The Hessian\nbound in part (i) follows immediately from (1.1); the\nPoincaré and covariance bounds then follow from the standard\nlog-concavity facts (D.6) and\nLemma D.3 in Appendix D, applied with\n$m=\\alpha+\\eta^{-1}$ and $L=\\beta+\\eta^{-1}$. The\nmarginal curvature bound in part (ii) is derived in\nAppendix D, at (D.10). The\nreflection statement follows directly from (2.6)."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.E1",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3551,
      "line_end": 3558,
      "byte_start": 717553,
      "byte_end": 719703,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.E1.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "1f2c060d3d5cadb913d3707396a03d12fcbee241933e4bdc134beac774b8f18f",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$(\\mathsf{P}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int f(x^{\\prime},y)\\,\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})=\\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\\mid Y=y]\\,.$\n\n(B.1)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.E2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3561,
      "line_end": 3570,
      "byte_start": 720477,
      "byte_end": 724025,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.E2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "2a3ed85e38715b4d6c91c8dbfb4a485c159c4511ad42beaded2a796d4bcdf30b",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\begin{split}\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P})=\\{f\\in\\mathfrak{H}:f(x,y)=g(y)\\text{ for some }g\\in L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})\\}\\,,\\\\\n\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\ker(\\mathsf{P})=\\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp})=\\{f\\in\\mathfrak{H}:\\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\\mid Y]=0\\}\\,.\\end{split}$\n\n(B.2)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.E3",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3585,
      "line_end": 3596,
      "byte_start": 728702,
      "byte_end": 732443,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.E3.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "7cb41b24f384991a849eef67e263bfcf9b3b2903b8a6c8dbef78020da9beb8b2",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\mathsf{T}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}\\\\\n\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\begin{aligned} \\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,,\\\\\n\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,.\\end{aligned}$\n\n(B.3)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.E4",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3605,
      "line_end": 3612,
      "byte_start": 734351,
      "byte_end": 735917,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.E4.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "bd93f2e460e4f59aa562b2ba13e36ad16cd810424677c8b114e6a93474fc65b8",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$(\\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq f(\\mathsf{U}(x,y))=f(x,2x-y)\\,.$\n\n(B.4)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.E5",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3628,
      "line_end": 3635,
      "byte_start": 740263,
      "byte_end": 742291,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.E5.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "fe258f4f7d272a57a2fa1293a3b4663924b5a3e556f87f1ce03cd28a3837f959",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\,.$\n\n(B.5)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.SS2.p2.2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3725,
      "line_end": 3727,
      "byte_start": 764254,
      "byte_end": 765723,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.SS2.p2.2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "5334447b246d2e9ec12b0bbc26da06456d593d5621898e991558cd2f2ccad78c",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "The pair $(Y_{+},Y_{-})$ is exchangeable. We henceforth identify\n$\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}$ with $L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})$ and write $f(y)$ for a\nmacroscopic observable. Under this identification,"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.E8",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3717,
      "line_end": 3724,
      "byte_start": 762524,
      "byte_end": 764253,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.E8.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "5a60b7a7667ec1a06d63f370f1711890038e27cb223b63d17031494e7ee0928a",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$Y_{+}\\coloneqq X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptY_{-}\\coloneqq X-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptZ\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptX\\sim\\mu\\,.$\n\n(B.8)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.E9",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3728,
      "line_end": 3735,
      "byte_start": 765724,
      "byte_end": 768134,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.E9.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "d24fec695423a3d6af884a8a3fe3c46804b6e817f935fb89b1853a6ab5f65241",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f)(y)=\\mathbb{E}[f(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+}=y]\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\mathbb{E}\\Var(f(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+})\\,.$\n\n(B.9)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.E10",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3740,
      "line_end": 3747,
      "byte_start": 768975,
      "byte_end": 770419,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.E10.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "7b09ee8258f3e6c4ecc506e9513ec8256e0d1f4083f38b545d6c1dd03486c0fb",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\\hskip 10.00002pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\,.$\n\n(B.10)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.SS2.p3.2",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3748,
      "line_end": 3749,
      "byte_start": 770420,
      "byte_end": 771530,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.SS2.p3.2.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "74a2f422e540f4a4d51a4b26cc72672e31a4c2a8895173b07a70b487b0df30b1",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "By (B.5),\n$\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}$, and hence"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.E11",
      "source_id": "PBPS2609.06905v1",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "source standing objects, actual-law operator/variance contract, or explicit downstream boundary",
      "line_start": 3750,
      "line_end": 3757,
      "byte_start": 771531,
      "byte_end": 773654,
      "balanced_fragment": "A2.E11.balanced.html",
      "raw_sha256": "6d19997456600e603e6f081f055bf929069a5e636c8c8fa7d2cb37a8615428f7",
      "source_text_with_math_alttext": "$\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|=\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f\\|\\,,\\hskip 10.00002ptf\\in\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\,.$\n\n(B.11)"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1",
